{"kind":"report","text":"Approved: exact registration-switch head f004bb3b268e9f1ed5258b75158ae501d467ea02 on builder/oauth-registration-policy-20261103, tree e971d6c9, for request d7c3da24 under promise 3ff36d7b and review request 674fa9d1. This approval covers OAUTH_DYNAMIC_REGISTRATION, the default-off route, the metadata change and the lazy registry wrapper. It enables no deployed setting and claims no O4, G3 or Goose acceptance.\n\nScope. Main c55c59da is an ancestor, and the worktree is clean. Against main, the head changes oauth-clients.ts, oauth-routes.ts, the scope Worker, the Native OAuth test, the consent test, the security inventory and its test, docs/mcp.md, two security docs, the design, the note and four manifests. The commit-message check passes for all five commits. No card path changes. Page run 41637833087 succeeded at 450025c5, and only the note and the CI manifest change after it.\n\nWhat holds:\n\n- oauthPolicy accepts an unset setting as off and the exact string \"on\" as on. Any other value returns null, so mcpRoute, the consent page and the signed grant, connection-list and revoke-grant controls all answer 404 before any namespace lookup. The invalid-policy case checks \"off\", \"true\", \"ON\", the empty string and \" on\" on all eleven routes.\n- With registration off, POST /oauth/register returns the fixed 400 invalid_client_metadata right after the method check. It reads no body, checks no content type and obtains no registry. The new case trips on a body read or a namespace lookup, and it finds neither.\n- Issuer metadata omits registration_endpoint when registration is off and names it when it is on.\n- The Worker now builds the registry stub inside registerClient and resolveClient. Metadata and the off route therefore never reach the registry object.\n- Metadata-document clients keep the whole flow with registration off: the HTTPS document fetch, PKCE, signed control, Native enrollment, code exchange, replay refusal, refresh rotation and revocation. Both metadata cases fetch the document once and leave the registration rows exactly as they found them. The two original routed cases still run with registration on, including the own-agent retention race.\n- Existing registered clients, redirect and origin checks, token lifetimes, grant retention and Native authority are unchanged.\n- Control 08 removes the off-route guard, and control 09 removes the invalid-value guard. Each fails its intended case without a timeout, and each names a baseline equal to the exact file at the head: cd34591a… for oauth-routes.ts and 7ece6f05… for oauth-clients.ts. Both restore the source.\n- No Wrangler file sets the new value. Every Worker therefore starts with registration off at its next deploy.\n\nThe gate. Ruling fdeb2ade, ratified as 990fa38b, lets me assess the sealed record. The record is enough for this change, and the gate stays failed. gate.exit at 5183640a reads exit 1 after 1,520 seconds. source-before and source-after both record tree 4d044822 and a clean status. Every precheck and the kernel, Node 133, Counting 56 and plain 3,601 stages pass. Native records 1,063 passed, 2 failed and 2 skipped, with zero unhandled errors. My reasons:\n\n- The consent failure follows from this change. The test expected 201 from registration and got the new default 400. The repair is one line: it adds OAUTH_DYNAMIC_REGISTRATION: \"on\" to that test's local Worker environment. Every case and assertion stays, nothing imports the file, and the complete owner passes with its compiler. From the gate commit to the head, only that line, the note and three manifests change.\n- The archive-scale failure is not this change's. This head changes no archive source, test, bound or deadline, and the owner's bytes match the gate. The owner passes once alone in 209 seconds. The planner's request 64552d40 now tracks it as a possible fault under load. I agree it should not hold this head.\n- The new Native OAuth cases passed inside the frozen gate itself, so the gate ran the change's own witnesses on committed source.\n- The gate reports no EnvironmentTeardownError, so df2abe35 stays closed.\n\nEvidence. The four manifests hash to 55ef3f16…, ec856c0f…, dc890fcf… and e9ac11ae…, and the note names all four. All 39 public files match their sizes and digests and are read-only, every SHA256SUMS file matches, and no unit holds an unlisted file. All 59 private files match their indexes. The focused checks ran on the uncommitted change over d7f1ebf7, as their record says. The frozen gate covers the committed source. The scan for private keys, GitHub tokens and bearer values finds no match.\n\nArchitecture: sound. One policy object carries the setting, and every OAuth entry point already reads that object.\n\nSecurity: no blocking finding. Default-off removes the anonymous registration write that drove finding 35b3a7a0, and a mistyped value closes the routes instead of opening registration. Two points for the planner:\n\n1. After the next deploy, a host that cannot present an allowlisted metadata document cannot connect. O4 must use metadata-document clients from claude.ai and chatgpt.com, as the note plans.\n2. Enabling registration on a hosted Worker still needs the per-address rate limit first, as docs/mcp.md now states.\n\nSimplification: no required change.","body":{"artifact":"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:a57c43478151c6a0296eeb9bca42270dd71169a0","binding":"assigned","head":"f004bb3b268e9f1ed5258b75158ae501d467ea02","head_news_acknowledged":"[\"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:9c08ed9d17455982e6d5494d945469be01121f8d\"]","implementations":"[\"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:3ff36d7b82ee05d621f3e0f68fd7a0c2211312aa\"]","review_frontier":"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:67c9eb5fbfc5e1213732fe367217234b9f342217","review_path":"reviewguard@1","verdict":"approved"}}